  "reason": "Evidence: The best configuration so far is config_018 (scvi_n200 + imagenet_vit_l + avgpool + weighted, acc=0.706, cost=4.82 GPU hrs), which clearly outperforms all other tested setups. Both scvi_n200 and imagenet_vit_l are consistently superior to their alternatives. The remaining untested variation within this top encoder pair is the aggregation method: all completed experiments use avgpool, so we haven't tested whether transformer aggregation can capture richer inter-profile interactions. This experiment (config_024: scvi_n200, imagenet_vit_l, transformer, weighted) isolates the aggregation change while keeping the proven weighted fusion, directly testing whether attention-based profile aggregation can push accuracy beyond 0.706. It is the highest-value exploitation step: it extends the single best result along the most promising unexplored axis. Expected relative cost: moderate increase over config_018 (est. ~6-9 GPU hrs) due to transformer attention over profiles, but the vit_l encoder dominates training cost so the increment is manageable. With 5 experiments remaining, this balances the risk of a large cost spike against the high probability of meaningful accuracy gain."
}

